---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import LegalArticle from "../components/LegalArticle.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Terms of Use - Diald Club"
  description="Terms of Use for the Diald Club coffee tracking app."
  bodyClass="legal-page"
>
  <LegalArticle title="Terms of Use" updated="4 July 2026">
    <p>
      These Terms of Use apply to your use of the Diald Club iOS app and
      website. By using Diald, you agree to these terms and to Apple's standard
      End User License Agreement (EULA) for apps distributed through the App
      Store.
    </p>

    <h2>Apple standard EULA</h2>
    <p>
      Diald uses Apple's standard EULA. You can review it at <a
        href="https://www.apple.com/legal/internet-services/itunes/dev/stdeula/"
        >apple.com/legal/internet-services/itunes/dev/stdeula/</a
      >.
    </p>

    <h2>Subscriptions</h2>
    <p>
      Diald offers an optional auto-renewable subscription named Supporter
      Monthly. Subscription pricing and duration are shown in the app before
      purchase and are confirmed by Apple's purchase sheet.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>Payment is charged to your Apple ID after purchase confirmation.</li>
      <li>
        The subscription renews automatically unless canceled at least 24 hours
        before the end of the current period.
      </li>
      <li>
        Your Apple ID account is charged for renewal within 24 hours before the
        end of the current period.
      </li>
      <li>
        You can manage or cancel your subscription in your App Store account
        settings.
      </li>
      <li>
        Canceling a subscription stops future renewal; it does not remove access
        already paid for during the current period.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Accounts and your content</h2>
    <p>
      You are responsible for keeping your account secure and for the beans,
      brews, recipes, steps, ratings, notes, reminders, and other content you
      add to Diald. Do not upload, enter, or share content that you do not have
      the right to use.
    </p>

    <h2>Free and paid access</h2>
    <p>
      Diald may limit some features for free accounts, including the number of
      brew extractions that can be logged. Paid subscription access unlocks the
      features described in the app at the time of purchase.
    </p>

    <h2>AI features</h2>
    <p>
      AI analysis is optional and requires you to provide your own API key for
      the provider you choose. You are responsible for your use of that
      provider, including any provider charges, limits, terms, and privacy
      practices. AI output may be incomplete or inaccurate and should be treated
      as guidance rather than professional advice.
    </p>

    <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
    <p>
      Do not misuse the service, interfere with its operation, attempt
      unauthorized access, reverse engineer protected service components, or use
      Diald to violate laws or the rights of others.
    </p>

    <h2>Third-party services</h2>
    <p>
      Diald uses third-party services including Supabase for authentication and
      data storage, Apple services for App Store purchases and notifications,
      Google and Apple for sign-in when selected, and OpenAI or Anthropic when
      you choose to run AI analysis. Your use of those services may also be
      governed by their own terms and policies.
    </p>

    <h2>Service changes</h2>
    <p>
      We may change, suspend, or discontinue features as the app evolves. We
      will not intentionally remove paid access during a paid subscription
      period except where required for security, legal, or platform compliance
      reasons.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes to these terms</h2>
    <p>
      We may update these terms from time to time. When we do, we will revise
      the "Last updated" date above. Continued use of the app after changes take
      effect constitutes acceptance of the updated terms.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact us</h2>
    <p>
      If you have questions about these terms, contact us at <a
        href="mailto:kyle@kylescudder.co.uk">kyle@kylescudder.co.uk</a
      >.
    </p>
  </LegalArticle>
</BaseLayout>
